            "review_title": "Review at Nha Hang 241",
            "review_text": "Mah_Murrini\n467 contributions\n0\nA real locals' restaurant\nAug 2015\nSince our hotel (Nikko) is just around the corner, we walked by two days in a row before we decided to try it. It was bustling with locals both times. As we speak no Vietnamese and they spoke no English, we ordered our favorite Vietnamese soup, Pho Tai. It was delicious, and they had a couple of greens, along with the usual basil, that I have not seen stateside. Oh, and it was only 60,000 dong (around US $3) for two bowls and they refused our tip!\n\nIf you want to finish off with a strong yet really tasty iced coffee, I highly recommend Little Owl across the street. No frills or food, and again no English, just deliciousness in a glass.\nRead more\nWritten August 6, 2015",
