            "review_title": "Review at Nha Hang 241",
            "review_text": "John M\nBurntisland, United Kingdom26 contributions\n0\nEat like a local\nOct 2012 • Family\nI have visited this restaurant many times over a number of years and it has never disappointed. It serves a fairly standard range of Vietnamese cuisine, nothing too startling.\n\nThe service is generally top notch, with one server assigned to maybe two or three tables at busy times, and more servers/table when quiet.\n\nThe standard of food is very good. For foodies it is probably not the very top of the range, but I have found all the dishes I have tried to be of consistently good quality. The menu is pretty extensive and I'd recommend ordering anything that takes your fancy as the pricing is very reasonable. \n\nI think the thing that keeps me coming back is the atmosphere, which is a pleasant retreat from the hectic streets without trying too hard to join the upmarket eateries. It is almost always very quiet at lunchtime, especially upstairs, and is a great place for a relaxing lunch with a few beers. Alternatively head there of an evening and eat amongst an almost exclusively Vietnamese clientele.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 17, 2013",
